    "html": "<p>A weather balloon is filled with a sample of ideal gas. At the Earth's surface, the pressure of the gas is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> and its absolute temperature is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span>. The balloon rises to a height where the gas pressure is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.20P\"></span> and the absolute temperature is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.80T\"></span>. What is the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\text{final volume}}{\\text{initial volume}}\"></span> of the gas?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.16\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.25\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.0\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\"></span></p></li></ol>"
